      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KRAKARIB (6) fitter now third up. Slow into stride and got further back than anticipated with a poor eighth over 1000m at the Sunshine Coast. Ready for this trip and can return to form if he jumps cleanly. OAKFIELD DUKE (2) tough old gelding who gets better with age. Rewarded for his consistency third up with a slick victory over 1200m at Coffs Harbour. Can offset the weight increase from the good gate. Each way. THE WOLF (4) goes well a this track and finally drawn a decent gate. Can take control early and regular rider hops back aboard. Set to give this a shake. SIR CARTER (3) much better effort second up with a solid fifth over 1200m at Coffs Harbour. Can hold a forward position and deserves another chance.",
